# Frontend — web (`@nucleify/web`)

Landing Nuxt app. Source in `web/src/`. Shared code comes from `shared_modules/`.

## Structure

```
web/src/
├── pages/[lang]/     # Thin route wrappers
├── pages/home/       # Landing sections (migrated from nuc_pages)
├── plugins/          # nucleify-ui + registerNuc*
├── server/api/       # Nitro gateway catch-all
├── assets/           # SCSS entry (imports from shared_modules)
└── nucleify.ts       # Re-exports shared_modules + flashToast
```

## Conventions

- UI: `nui-*` from `nucleify-ui` (Lit web components)
- Vue SFCs: `<script setup lang="ts">`
- Import shared via `shared_modules/nuc_*/…` or `modules` alias
- Do not place shared code under `web/`

## Portable UI (`*.nuc.tsx`)

Author portable presentational UI in `*.nuc.tsx` (not Vue/React APIs). The compiler emits sibling `.vue` / `.tsx` (+ `.css`). Do not hand-edit emit as source of truth — use `pnpm compiler -- import` after emit edits. Bundlers ignore `*.nuc.tsx`; see `compiler/PORTABLE.md` and `compiler/README.md`.
